# CLAUDE.md

This machine's setup, conventions, and detailed documentation live in **[AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md)**.

Read `AGENTS.md` first. It is the canonical entry point and indexes everything
under [`docs/`](./docs/).

This file exists only to point there, so that both Claude Code and any other
agent tooling converge on the same source of truth. Do not duplicate content
here — edit `AGENTS.md` or the relevant file in `docs/` instead.

`~/AGENTS.md` and `~/docs` are symlinks. The files themselves live in
`~/dev/machines/{{ .chezmoi.hostname }}/`, which syncs to Nextcloud so each machine's docs are
available from every machine. `~/me` also points there. See `~/dev/README.md`
for the layout, and note that working git clones belong in `~/repos` — never
in `~/dev`, which is a sync root.
